==> omaddons robot-docs install-skill -h <==
Install the agent guide as a coding agent's skill

Usage: omaddons robot-docs install-skill [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dir <DIR>  The skill folder to write SKILL.md into

Examples:
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill  into ~/.claude/skills/omaddons
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill --dir ~/.codex/skills/omaddons

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons robot-docs install-skill --help <==
Install the agent guide as a coding agent's skill

As SKILL.md, where coding agents load skills.

Usage: omaddons robot-docs install-skill [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dir <DIR>
          The skill folder to write SKILL.md into
          
          Default: $HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons. It is created when its parent exists.

Examples:
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill              for Claude Code
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill --dry-run    what it would write
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill --dir $HOME/.codex/skills/omaddons

Writes the agent guide, the same bytes as omaddons robot-docs guide, as SKILL.md in
the skill folder. The default needs $HOME/.claude and creates skills/omaddons in it; a
--dir folder is created when its parent exists. A SKILL.md you edited is kept as
SKILL.md.bak, or SKILL.md.bak.1, .2 and so on: an earlier backup is never replaced. A
SKILL.md that is a symlink is refused; a symlinked folder is followed and judged where it
points. It never writes into a game client, a Wine prefix or omaddons' own folders.
omaddons doctor reports an installed skill that holds another guide than this build's.
Remove the skill by deleting the folder.

See also: robot-docs guide, doctor

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
